WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:03.750
- Our next guest didn't start
dancing until she was 13

00:00:03.750 --> 00:00:04.960
and then rose to become

00:00:04.960 --> 00:00:07.980
the first ever African
American Principal Dancer

00:00:07.980 --> 00:00:10.470
of the American Ballet
Theater, not too shabby.

00:00:10.470 --> 00:00:12.930
She is a trailblazer and a true icon.

00:00:12.930 --> 00:00:15.758
Please, welcome Misty Copeland, everybody.

00:00:15.758 --> 00:00:19.762
(blues music)
(clapping and applause)

00:00:19.762 --> 00:00:21.380
Hi, it's good to see you again.

00:00:21.380 --> 00:00:23.710
We talked over Zoom in the summer.

00:00:23.710 --> 00:00:26.370
- Yes, it's so good to see you as well.

00:00:26.370 --> 00:00:28.740
And thank you for all
of the incredible work

00:00:28.740 --> 00:00:29.810
you're doing through your show.

00:00:29.810 --> 00:00:32.600
It's really impressive,
and I'm happy to be back.

00:00:32.600 --> 00:00:34.540
- Oh man, thank you so much, and I,

00:00:34.540 --> 00:00:35.640
you know, it's a little sad

00:00:35.640 --> 00:00:37.880
as I thought the next
time you'd be on my show,

00:00:37.880 --> 00:00:38.990
you'd be here physically,

00:00:38.990 --> 00:00:40.620
but we still can't do that quite yet.

00:00:40.620 --> 00:00:42.660
So (laughs) there's that,

00:00:42.660 --> 00:00:44.120
toast to that.
- We'll get there.

00:00:44.120 --> 00:00:47.330
- We're gonna get there,
I have to keep saying it.

00:00:47.330 --> 00:00:49.322
So representation though,
on a serious note,

00:00:49.322 --> 00:00:50.530
it's super important.

00:00:50.530 --> 00:00:52.170
Not only to you, but to me as well.

00:00:52.170 --> 00:00:55.300
So, how is that true for you, as a girl?

00:00:55.300 --> 00:00:57.840
- Yeah, you know, it's been really

00:00:58.710 --> 00:01:02.180
important for me to have
that representation.

00:01:02.180 --> 00:01:04.070
I think it was Mariah Carey

00:01:04.070 --> 00:01:07.740
that really was the first person that,

00:01:07.740 --> 00:01:09.390
I saw myself in.

00:01:09.390 --> 00:01:13.350
She was a biracial
woman who was succeeding

00:01:13.350 --> 00:01:14.900
and was extremely talented.

00:01:14.900 --> 00:01:16.850
And the power in seeing her

00:01:16.850 --> 00:01:19.400
when I was seven years old
when she first came out,

00:01:20.480 --> 00:01:22.790
it it's this amazing through line

00:01:22.790 --> 00:01:25.530
where I can understand
the benefits of just

00:01:25.530 --> 00:01:27.440
having my presence on the stage,

00:01:27.440 --> 00:01:31.208
what it can do for an entire community.

00:01:31.208 --> 00:01:36.170
It's, so powerful in a way
that I think we often overlook

00:01:36.170 --> 00:01:38.430
or forget for children to see themselves

00:01:38.430 --> 00:01:40.500
represented in spaces they might

00:01:40.500 --> 00:01:43.570
not otherwise consider themselves being.

00:01:43.570 --> 00:01:46.050
- Yeah, it's so interesting
'cause we grew up differently.

00:01:46.050 --> 00:01:47.800
But Mariah was also one for me,

00:01:47.800 --> 00:01:49.930
not just as a singer, but as a writer.

00:01:49.930 --> 00:01:51.280
I thought it was interesting her story,

00:01:51.280 --> 00:01:53.530
how she kind of, came from,

00:01:53.530 --> 00:01:54.800
you know, very humble beginnings

00:01:54.800 --> 00:01:56.400
of kind of a broken home
and this whole thing.

00:01:56.400 --> 00:01:57.840
And I kind of related to a lot of that.

00:01:57.840 --> 00:02:00.770
So it's interesting how, people
in the public eye can just

00:02:00.770 --> 00:02:03.050
totally have this huge impact
on you as a little kid.

00:02:03.050 --> 00:02:05.290
And, I just thought it
was very interesting but.

00:02:05.290 --> 00:02:06.770
So I didn't know this,

00:02:06.770 --> 00:02:08.290
but Prince actually had

00:02:08.290 --> 00:02:10.020
an early kind of impact on your career,

00:02:10.020 --> 00:02:11.050
right?
- Yeah.

00:02:11.050 --> 00:02:11.890
- That's the coolest thing ever.

00:02:11.890 --> 00:02:13.580
- A lot of people (laughs)

00:02:13.580 --> 00:02:15.120
I know, yeah.

00:02:15.120 --> 00:02:16.790
It seems really random,

00:02:16.790 --> 00:02:21.790
but Prince has always had
a love of other artists,

00:02:22.510 --> 00:02:26.300
and as well as dancers,
throughout his career.

00:02:26.300 --> 00:02:28.980
But he came into my life.

00:02:28.980 --> 00:02:31.470
I was a Soloist in American Ballet Theater

00:02:31.470 --> 00:02:34.750
and he was just really adamant about me

00:02:34.750 --> 00:02:37.000
starring in this music video of his.

00:02:37.000 --> 00:02:40.160
And, it was really random
and out of the blue,

00:02:40.160 --> 00:02:42.230
but I ended up touring with him on and off

00:02:42.230 --> 00:02:44.170
for about five years.

00:02:44.170 --> 00:02:47.620
And, you know, he was such a supporter

00:02:47.620 --> 00:02:50.830
and so extremely charitable to ballet

00:02:50.830 --> 00:02:54.160
and to so many different
schools and companies

00:02:54.160 --> 00:02:56.510
that I'm passionate about and,

00:02:56.510 --> 00:02:57.560
you know, behind the scenes,

00:02:57.560 --> 00:02:58.980
he was doing a lot of incredible work

00:02:58.980 --> 00:03:00.970
and he'd show up to a
lot of my performances

00:03:00.970 --> 00:03:02.510
and people wouldn't even know he was

00:03:02.510 --> 00:03:05.200
up there in the balcony, watching

00:03:05.200 --> 00:03:09.310
just, he really truly believed
in the next generation

00:03:09.310 --> 00:03:13.380
and nurturing them to be more
than artists like himself.

00:03:13.380 --> 00:03:15.070
- I think too, like I never got to meet up

00:03:15.070 --> 00:03:17.130
every artist I know that has

00:03:17.130 --> 00:03:18.700
been impacted by him like in person,

00:03:18.700 --> 00:03:21.950
like personally has a
relationship or worked with him.

00:03:21.950 --> 00:03:23.720
I think he just had such a true,

00:03:23.720 --> 00:03:27.820
like deep kind of love for
music and the arts in general.

00:03:27.820 --> 00:03:29.170
So I think that was kind of,

00:03:29.170 --> 00:03:30.050
'cause whenever I found out

00:03:30.050 --> 00:03:31.417
that you were in one of
his shows, I was like,

00:03:31.417 --> 00:03:32.440
"That doesn't seem weird to me.

00:03:32.440 --> 00:03:33.460
That seems very Prince."

00:03:33.460 --> 00:03:36.368
Like he'd have a prima
ballerina in his show.

00:03:36.368 --> 00:03:37.670
(laughter)
Anyway

00:03:37.670 --> 00:03:40.440
but tell us about your
current social campaign,

00:03:40.440 --> 00:03:41.930
Show Some Muscle.

00:03:41.930 --> 00:03:44.990
- I'm so excited about it.

00:03:44.990 --> 00:03:46.660
I think that, you know,

00:03:46.660 --> 00:03:50.240
looking at Ford and looking
at a muscle car, which is,

00:03:50.240 --> 00:03:52.170
you know, what is a part of this campaign,

00:03:52.170 --> 00:03:54.650
the Mustang Mach-E.

00:03:54.650 --> 00:03:56.770
I don't think you would think of women

00:03:56.770 --> 00:03:58.480
especially a ballerina being attached.

00:03:58.480 --> 00:04:02.540
But, the Show Some Muscle
campaign that they have is really,

00:04:02.540 --> 00:04:05.370
you know, me encouraging other women

00:04:05.370 --> 00:04:08.460
to share their stories of
strength and perseverance.

00:04:08.460 --> 00:04:11.520
And that strength doesn't
have to be physical strength

00:04:11.520 --> 00:04:15.300
in this outward, masculinity that,

00:04:15.300 --> 00:04:18.080
you know, first of all, having a woman

00:04:18.080 --> 00:04:22.610
be behind designing this
car, an electric car,

00:04:22.610 --> 00:04:24.860
is so empowering to show,

00:04:24.860 --> 00:04:27.770
you know, the next generation
to show little girls

00:04:27.770 --> 00:04:29.380
all that we're capable of.

00:04:29.380 --> 00:04:30.213
And so,

00:04:30.213 --> 00:04:32.550
you know, show some muscle to me means,

00:04:32.550 --> 00:04:36.760
you know, this inner strength
that so many women have

00:04:36.760 --> 00:04:39.310
and especially as a ballerina, you know?

00:04:39.310 --> 00:04:41.880
Of course we have to have
the physical abilities

00:04:41.880 --> 00:04:43.590
to do what we do on stage

00:04:43.590 --> 00:04:45.960
but to be able to make it
look effortless and easy

00:04:45.960 --> 00:04:48.740
is definitely showing some inner strength

00:04:48.740 --> 00:04:49.610
and showing some muscle.

00:04:49.610 --> 00:04:51.160
- Yeah, I think that's really cool.

00:04:51.160 --> 00:04:53.510
I also, I love electric
cars also love muscle cars.

00:04:53.510 --> 00:04:55.520
So see, girls (mumbles)

00:04:55.520 --> 00:04:59.150
- Yeah, this is the car for you.

00:04:59.150 --> 00:05:00.410
- I love that.

00:05:00.410 --> 00:05:04.353
Well, everybody check out
#showsomemuscle on social media.

